{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_017faa0cbaaf43ee23a1d3ec997a9dfb42a1d566b7437d275029ac48a5b64949","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_96494452e8e6dec1c0dd7b7b4045811b4a369f67840b09b11ed6b58d0039cdb9"],"source_ids":["src_7a0a58936ecc5662b59e0741d37b912f"],"text":"Every session gets construct's MCP tools, letting any harness spawn subagents, send them input, and read their output for agent-to-agent orchestration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_02011da69bbf74c81888bbae3faca43846633aa9a8c78a4f06a1e71fb4cdc6c2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_88df3751d9ac69b4d42a66c8f4f8e6cd1eaa8b0d7c47a2d1ce122c0a3118a5a4","slc_9e84ded9781e976114b062dde1cb89b97fd4fd982292c206bdbde2413ff24b8f"],"source_ids":["src_7a0a58936ecc5662b59e0741d37b912f"],"text":"Construct wraps CLIs already on the machine; users must install and authenticate harnesses such as codex, claude, opencode, agy, grok, muse, and prime-agent, while smith is built in.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_127af993f42400a88dd4141a77e2e2c5e02f31dad4eed105f7fe14e6e3dcd847","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5019dc8519656fe93bd8aac6f4a642b2d54df36013a634e5c652b75d06c8c54f"],"source_ids":["src_7a0a58936ecc5662b59e0741d37b912f"],"text":"Lineage lets sessions branch like ideas: a session can be forked for a parallel attempt, including cross-harness forks, and results merged back.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_161bcf4eddb511af5b2f7ff00ae51ed2c69e4692e7f4292ab68abd5b64b771ab","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5019dc8519656fe93bd8aac6f4a642b2d54df36013a634e5c652b75d06c8c54f"],"source_ids":["src_7a0a58936ecc5662b59e0741d37b912f"],"text":"Sessions live in the daemon rather than the terminal, so SSH drops or laptop sleep do not stop agents, and users can reattach with scrollback intact.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1eca237c3520f8342d800282c4ad374bc38ecc2dcb9c110ec69fa8c2f95fcd42","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_260f5d843d365e4fec4d3f6e8c83fb396c289887de9f56f6168cc535232351da"],"source_ids":["src_7a0a58936ecc5662b59e0741d37b912f"],"text":"`/remote-control` opens a browser-accessible web client with a QR code so users can connect from a phone without service signup or setup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_296548d6b664097c80f0efa5d78661e0d361c1ec3a7ccf9f814c56a2429c03af","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5138899664a37c08718924d0a4a70fbd31e0d352992d4f3ddaa49f577297815a","slc_621d2437e679521b8e6d2f0a19dec67bd2209236b665b825db9370230362f465","slc_ab3a2f7456d68b18144d822c8f7d23457ba3ea5ceb8ca67c55df570e058868a3"],"source_ids":["src_5099209dfb4b55099db1adde99c6b52f"],"text":"Repository development practice: TUI demo clips are recorded deterministically with vhs against isolated per-recording daemon state directories, then verified with a midpoint frame before attaching to the PR.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3ffc63cbc0879acdda1390af2392c9e6e1b71bf70bc50be7b539ca1d18fd655e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0213b0f5dbee8e4c6d8abeec3e99821c1543d056cfc6b52a476655e676287052","slc_156ed70d4ffcce236a51593727dfbd8e1333ac7318a0f9ab575b242a6df16b10"],"source_ids":["src_7a0a58936ecc5662b59e0741d37b912f"],"text":"The daemon owns sessions, persists state, and exposes the local IPC socket used by clients; lifecycle helpers include daemon start/stop/restart with session-safe stop variants.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4d9c60a321fbb971b5ef835cfab111699ffb331093beebdc2ad24b6dccb01067","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"construct-worlds/construct@cf75b7398c78 snapshot c959755ce3b13c69","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c3aab37459df30d26170e1062715c9073d5313d3daa2e8a8692265e8741e6d70"],"source_ids":["src_7a0a58936ecc5662b59e0741d37b912f"],"text":"The harness adapter protocol uses separate adapter processes speaking JSON-RPC over stdio, so new tools can plug in without changing the daemon.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ba954430b879456fa1e6599cb581e387"}
